WEBVTT

00:15.670 --> 00:18.500
I never dreamed before

00:18.500 --> 00:21.340
I'm gonna knock the door

00:21.340 --> 00:24.910
into the world of perfect free

00:24.910 --> 00:27.010
(You ain't no lonely!)

00:27.010 --> 00:29.850
You're gonna say I'm lying

00:29.850 --> 00:32.580
I'm gonna get the chance

00:32.580 --> 00:36.150
I thought a chance is far from me

00:36.150 --> 00:37.320
(You ain't no lonely!)

00:37.320 --> 00:40.230
I was made to hit in America

00:40.230 --> 00:43.090
(I was made to hit in America)

00:43.090 --> 00:49.000
I was made to hit in America

00:49.000 --> 00:52.670
You are the sun, you are the star

00:52.670 --> 00:54.670
(To me, forever)

00:54.670 --> 00:58.380
You are the sun, you are the star

00:58.380 --> 01:01.610
(To me, forever)

01:08.450 --> 01:14.060
I was made to hit in America

01:14.060 --> 01:16.900
I was made to hit in America

01:16.900 --> 01:19.760
(I was made to hit in America)

01:19.760 --> 01:22.570
I was made to hit in America

01:22.570 --> 01:25.340
(I was made to hit in America)

01:25.340 --> 01:33.210
I was made to hit in America

02:17.790 --> 02:19.480
"Fishing Hole"

02:30.740 --> 02:32.500
Damn...

02:43.050 --> 02:48.010
"Live 19
'Blues'"

02:50.550 --> 02:54.390
He's probably walking Beck.

02:54.390 --> 02:57.060
For two days?

02:57.060 --> 02:59.490
He hasn't contacted you...

03:02.560 --> 03:03.860
Maybe...

03:07.240 --> 03:10.400
Hey, Grandma, aren't you worried?!

03:14.740 --> 03:15.730
No thanks...

03:18.580 --> 03:20.510
Looks like Lucille's gone, too.

03:24.750 --> 03:26.380
That guy...

03:49.880 --> 03:55.220
He wants to go to Kyoto...
Leon-san seems quite fond of Japan.

03:55.220 --> 03:59.720
Yeah...I heard he was
influenced by his uncle.

03:59.720 --> 04:01.190
Oh?

04:02.220 --> 04:06.060
His uncle took him in when
he was little, and raised him.

04:06.060 --> 04:08.790
Seems his uncle's wife was Japanese.

04:10.230 --> 04:15.070
Leon-san has overcome much
in order to succeed, I guess.

04:15.070 --> 04:17.070
I don't know the details,

04:17.070 --> 04:21.080
but I hear he's got the blood
of five continents in his veins-

04:21.080 --> 04:24.610
including Asian, Anglo-Saxon and African.

04:24.610 --> 04:27.080
Five?

04:27.080 --> 04:30.050
Of course, it's just a rumor.

04:31.750 --> 04:34.880
-I find him a little scary.
-Yeah...

04:52.540 --> 04:55.180
Hi, Boss...

04:55.180 --> 04:57.550
Well, I'm here myself.

04:57.550 --> 05:01.000
I guess everyone is shopping
in Akihabara right now.

05:02.050 --> 05:03.380
That man?

05:03.380 --> 05:05.820
That's fine.

05:05.820 --> 05:07.720
I beat the hell outta him.

05:08.890 --> 05:11.920
He won't even think
of running away from us.

05:13.390 --> 05:16.230
Okay, 10 o'clock. Tokyo Station?

05:16.230 --> 05:18.360
I'll pick you up on time, Boss.

05:34.920 --> 05:38.850
Fucking blood on my...I can't believe
this muthafucker hit me in the head!

05:38.850 --> 05:43.020
I'll kill you, little fucker!
Damn it! You really pissed me off!

05:54.540 --> 05:55.700
Mister Sykes...

05:55.700 --> 05:59.370
Do you know the guy
called John Lee Davis?

05:59.370 --> 06:01.380
He called you at the office.

06:01.380 --> 06:06.710
He's in Japan right now as
a backup band for a soul singer.

06:06.710 --> 06:10.220
Oh...I haven't seen him for three years...

06:10.220 --> 06:11.550
Oh?

06:11.550 --> 06:15.060
He, John Lee Davis, is my uncle.

06:15.060 --> 06:19.860
He must have gotten to know Mr. Sykes'
coming to Japan, by TV or something.

06:32.740 --> 06:35.910
Cross Road? That's classic...

06:35.910 --> 06:38.980
Is your uncle there at that restaurant?

06:38.980 --> 06:42.020
Yeah. He always goes there
when he visits Japan.

06:42.020 --> 06:46.350
I see. Anyway Boss,
why do we wanna bring him?

06:46.350 --> 06:48.690
Punk ass never does anything, anywhere.

06:48.690 --> 06:53.360
I told him that we found the Lucille,
and that a Japanese musician stole it.

06:53.360 --> 06:55.700
And now, he wants to see him.

06:55.700 --> 06:57.290
Isn't it going to be too much trouble?

06:59.030 --> 07:00.970
How's that dog?

07:00.970 --> 07:03.370
Hmph...He'll never take to me.

07:41.180 --> 07:42.640
The blues...

07:44.350 --> 07:46.180
Sounds like Robert Johnson...

07:46.180 --> 07:47.350
Surprising...

07:47.350 --> 07:52.290
Money mad boss, Leon Sykes,
talk about Robert Johnson?

07:55.360 --> 07:57.360
Hey...Leon!

07:57.360 --> 08:00.860
Come on...What are you putting
on that dreadful face for?

08:00.860 --> 08:03.700
I wouldn't sue you for money
like your dad did.

08:03.700 --> 08:07.030
Come on, Leon. This is
your Uncle John Lee Davis!

08:08.370 --> 08:10.200
John...

08:10.200 --> 08:11.800
Leon...

08:17.040 --> 08:19.550
Is that the Japanese?

08:19.550 --> 08:22.720
Yeah. Ryusuke Minami.

08:22.720 --> 08:25.390
The fucked up punk
who used a picture of Lucille

08:25.390 --> 08:28.660
for the album jacket that was released
by an Indies label in Chicago.

08:28.660 --> 08:30.350
Say somethin'!

08:36.060 --> 08:38.330
I'm gonna go wash my hands.

08:38.330 --> 08:39.320
Yeah...

08:46.670 --> 08:49.510
I was listening to you play, earlier.

08:49.510 --> 08:52.680
Hey, brat...You still alive?

08:52.680 --> 08:55.440
You might be Mr. John Lee Davis?

09:09.860 --> 09:13.230
Good...Now what about this?

09:28.550 --> 09:32.390
That's from the gigs
in San Francisco, 1964.

09:32.390 --> 09:35.050
Hey...When were you born?

09:38.830 --> 09:41.950
Let me play with Mr. Davis, for my last...

09:49.840 --> 09:53.010
Can you play with hands like that?

09:53.010 --> 09:56.310
Fortunately...my left hand is fine.

10:45.330 --> 10:47.930
Yeah...

10:47.930 --> 10:50.330
The blues...It ain't all that bad.

10:50.330 --> 10:54.320
Not good for business.
Sure ain't gonna make us rich.

11:06.850 --> 11:10.350
Your guitar sound
reminds me of Sonny Boy.

11:10.350 --> 11:13.550
Is that right?

11:13.550 --> 11:16.190
Sonny Boy is my master.

11:16.190 --> 11:19.860
Jesus Christ! Then what about Lucille?

11:19.860 --> 11:23.030
Sonny Boy had no one to depend on...

11:23.030 --> 11:26.190
I was the only one who would
take Lucille on, after him.

11:27.540 --> 11:30.000
But I don't have what
it takes to own Lucille.

11:31.010 --> 11:36.040
So if the real Blues Man for Lucille
showed up, I'd've handed it over to him.

11:36.040 --> 11:38.010
You are the real Blues Man.

11:39.380 --> 11:41.380
I gave up the music scene once...

11:41.380 --> 11:44.370
I left Lucille to Leon, since then.

11:47.390 --> 11:51.890
Mr. John Lee Davis, it was
a great honor to play with you.

11:51.890 --> 11:53.120
Thank you.

11:54.730 --> 11:56.560
Doitashimashite.
("You're welcome")

12:08.580 --> 12:10.410
You want a cigarette?

12:10.410 --> 12:11.940
No, thanks.

12:20.590 --> 12:22.590
Leon, he is real.

12:22.590 --> 12:26.590
I've never seen any Japanese
who could express Blues that good.

12:26.590 --> 12:28.890
And on top of that, he's really young.

12:30.530 --> 12:32.570
Erica Blige has been murdered,

12:32.570 --> 12:35.470
and I heard rumor that you are the suspect.

12:35.470 --> 12:38.100
Erica had been critical of the RJ label.

12:40.710 --> 12:45.650
Leon...Would you kill
people for money, like this?

12:45.650 --> 12:47.080
He's too good to kill.

12:50.220 --> 12:55.520
Uncle...Even though you try to
live straight in this fucked up society...

12:55.520 --> 12:58.230
chances are, you'll die a loser.

12:58.230 --> 12:59.750
Most people die that way.

13:02.730 --> 13:04.360
So I...

13:13.910 --> 13:17.240
What a fucking cheesy fucked up music!

13:17.240 --> 13:19.110
Ouch!

13:32.360 --> 13:36.430
It's been four days since
Ryusuke-kun disappeared.

13:36.430 --> 13:37.870
Yeah...

13:37.870 --> 13:41.560
Maybe we should report it to the police.

13:43.040 --> 13:45.060
It's almost time for our performance.

13:48.310 --> 13:51.880
-I'll have the lady at the
fishing hole make a report.
-Hey!

13:51.880 --> 13:57.380
-Take a look at this! Hey!
-Huh? Chiba-kun!

13:57.380 --> 13:59.850
Uh...Has something happened?

14:01.560 --> 14:05.290
What...You two don't know about it?

14:07.730 --> 14:09.730
Ta-da!

14:09.730 --> 14:11.720
"Maho Minami"

14:09.730 --> 14:11.720
Ma...ho?

14:13.270 --> 14:13.730
"Maho Minami-Sparkling 16-year-old"

14:13.730 --> 14:15.970
"Maho Minami-Sparkling 16-year-old"

14:13.730 --> 14:15.970
Maho...Minami...

14:15.970 --> 14:16.400
Maho...Minami...

14:16.400 --> 14:17.770
Sixteen...

14:20.110 --> 14:21.610
"The moment the scent...
of excitement explodes."

14:20.110 --> 14:21.610
She might well become

14:21.610 --> 14:22.640
"The moment the scent...
of excitement explodes."

14:21.610 --> 14:22.640
An overnight sensation.

14:22.640 --> 14:23.380
An overnight sensation.

14:23.380 --> 14:24.110
"The moment the scent...
of excitement explodes."

14:25.580 --> 14:27.980
There are guys like you two all over
the nation, who'll be stuck on her.

14:27.980 --> 14:30.750
There are guys like you two all over
the nation, who'll be stuck on her.

14:30.750 --> 14:33.910
I-I'm not stuck on her!

14:35.760 --> 14:38.250
You can have it. See you!

14:39.360 --> 14:42.200
What are the two of you stuck on?

14:42.200 --> 14:46.530
Uh, just a book that explains how to
conquer computer games...I guess...

14:46.530 --> 14:48.200
Yeah, yeah...

14:48.200 --> 14:50.200
Oh?

14:50.200 --> 14:53.540
Didn't you hear about it
from Maho, Koyuki?

14:53.540 --> 14:57.410
I haven't seen her lately.
She seems busy...

15:02.880 --> 15:05.550
Oh, Saku-chan, you have a nosebleed.

15:05.550 --> 15:06.920
Ah!

15:11.890 --> 15:15.830
Oh, Taira-kun! What's up?

15:17.060 --> 15:19.400
What?!

15:19.400 --> 15:23.070
-What's the matter, Chiba-kun?!
-Yeah! I'll be right there!!

15:23.070 --> 15:25.270
-Oh...Chiba-kun!
-Oh...Chiba-kun!

15:28.580 --> 15:31.270
Hey! Ryusuke!

15:33.080 --> 15:34.410
Yo...

15:35.920 --> 15:40.020
He says he was out walking Beck.

15:40.020 --> 15:42.360
Why are you all bandaged up?

15:42.360 --> 15:44.860
Ryusuke-kun...Are you all right?

15:44.860 --> 15:46.690
Where were you?

15:46.690 --> 15:49.960
Where the heck are Beck and Lucille?!

15:51.370 --> 15:54.540
Well...Money and women...

15:54.540 --> 15:56.370
Don't ask awkward questions, will you?

15:56.370 --> 15:59.210
W-W-Women?

15:59.210 --> 16:00.610
Money?

16:01.980 --> 16:06.140
Anyway...Beck and Lucille
won't be coming back.

16:08.880 --> 16:10.880
-I'll go and talk to him.
-See you later.

16:10.880 --> 16:12.390
Yeah...

16:12.390 --> 16:14.720
Really, man...What were you doing?

16:14.720 --> 16:17.490
-Shut up, will you?
-Come on...Be nice.

16:19.560 --> 16:20.930
Ryusuke-kun...

16:23.900 --> 16:26.400
-It tastes a little different...
-Yeah...

16:26.400 --> 16:28.930
Boy, our boss is really...

16:37.340 --> 16:41.040
In other words...I wasn't worth killing.

16:50.360 --> 16:55.030
Yeah...That's right. I do kill for money.

16:55.030 --> 16:58.870
But I don't just murder people
for no reason.

16:58.870 --> 17:00.830
Now get the fuck outta here!

17:03.040 --> 17:07.840
Can someone like me create music
that will move people?

17:11.040 --> 17:13.210
What are you saying?!

17:13.210 --> 17:15.910
He's right! You're lucky to be alive!

17:17.720 --> 17:20.390
Hey, Saku! Look at this!!

17:20.390 --> 17:22.390
"Pro-Am Welcome Auditions!!"

17:20.390 --> 17:22.390
This would be a great chance!

17:22.390 --> 17:23.390
"Pro-Am Welcome Auditions!!"

17:23.390 --> 17:25.060
"Pro-Am Welcome Auditions!!"

17:23.390 --> 17:25.060
Ohh...Auditions!?

17:25.060 --> 17:27.390
Ohh...Auditions!?

17:27.390 --> 17:29.560
Let's tell Ryusuke-kun about it.

17:29.560 --> 17:31.570
Good idea!

17:31.570 --> 17:33.570
I don't know about that...

17:33.570 --> 17:35.400
-Huh?
-Uh...

17:35.400 --> 17:38.840
Those auditions were over two months ago.

17:38.840 --> 17:41.010
Huh? No way...

17:41.010 --> 17:45.180
Besides, bands prepare a whole year
for that Grateful Sound event.

17:45.180 --> 17:47.680
A-And you are?

17:47.680 --> 17:50.680
For your information,
the band that was chosen

17:50.680 --> 17:55.360
was a promising newcomer called
"La Majistol" on the Ran label.

17:55.360 --> 17:56.760
Ran...

17:56.760 --> 18:01.200
-In other words...
The contest was rigged.
-Uh, ma'am...

18:01.200 --> 18:04.360
-Ma'am?!
-This fishing hole is closed today.

18:08.370 --> 18:10.040
Huh?

18:10.040 --> 18:16.110
Y-Y-Y-You...Are you the boy who sang
with Dying Breed in that Jim Walsh movie?

18:16.110 --> 18:17.910
Yes. I am...

18:19.550 --> 18:22.880
This...This is you guys, right?

18:22.880 --> 18:24.050
Yes...

18:24.050 --> 18:29.050
Mongolian Chop Squad is the
name of our band in America.

18:31.060 --> 18:35.400
I did it! I finally found you!
I wasn't mistaken.

18:35.400 --> 18:39.660
My deductions were right,
after all! This is great!!

18:40.670 --> 18:43.840
Hey! Didn't I tell you
not to let customers in?!

18:43.840 --> 18:45.240
She's not a customer...

18:45.240 --> 18:49.010
I guess she is...but not really...

18:49.010 --> 18:54.070
-That lady heard our American CD
and used it to find us.

18:49.010 --> 18:54.070
-Eeek! I hooked something!
What should I do?!

18:55.080 --> 18:57.480
-That lady?

18:55.080 --> 18:57.480
-Somebody, help!

18:57.480 --> 19:00.520
Hm...Metal Glue...

19:00.520 --> 19:00.690
"Wao Sato-Metal Glue, Inc."

19:00.690 --> 19:04.020
"Wao Sato-Metal Glue, Inc."

19:00.690 --> 19:04.020
-Wa...o...Sato?
-Phew! It smells fishy...

19:04.020 --> 19:05.660
"Wao Sato-Metal Glue, Inc."

19:04.020 --> 19:05.660
-Here. Give it to me, please.
-Huh? Huh? What should I do?

19:05.660 --> 19:06.690
-Here. Give it to me, please.
-Huh? Huh? What should I do?

19:06.690 --> 19:10.360
-Hello?
-Hey, Ray...What the fuck're you doing?

19:10.360 --> 19:14.330
Oh! I'm sorry, I'm kinda busy...
Just a sec...

19:14.330 --> 19:15.900
Hey! Koyuki...

19:15.900 --> 19:17.770
Huh? What is it?

19:21.380 --> 19:22.780
Hello?

19:22.780 --> 19:23.880
Koyuki?

19:23.880 --> 19:26.380
Ryusuke-kun's back safely.

19:26.380 --> 19:29.720
He was probably over at some girl's.

19:29.720 --> 19:30.880
Never mind that...

19:30.880 --> 19:35.890
There's a sneak preview of the
Dying Breed tour movie today!

19:35.890 --> 19:39.330
What?! The Dying Breed movie?!

19:39.330 --> 19:40.330
Hello?

19:40.330 --> 19:43.160
Koyuki, you want to see it with me?

19:43.160 --> 19:45.000
-Yeah!
-Mm...

19:45.000 --> 19:48.840
-I gotta go...
-Yes! Go on!!

19:48.840 --> 19:50.500
Saku...

19:50.500 --> 19:53.200
Okay! Give this to Ryusuke-kun, will you?!

19:54.680 --> 19:56.140
How nice...

19:56.140 --> 19:57.700
He's enjoying his youth.

20:03.680 --> 20:04.840
You're late!

20:10.190 --> 20:12.790
I just got a call from Yoshito.

20:12.790 --> 20:15.860
He said he wanted to
see the movie too, so...

20:15.860 --> 20:21.700
Being with two guys...
isn't very good for Maho's future.

20:28.210 --> 20:30.710
Yoshito-kun, you want
to look at the program?

20:30.710 --> 20:34.380
I never read it before a movie.

20:34.380 --> 20:35.750
Oh...

20:40.150 --> 20:44.990
On the stage, they are perfect.
They're flawless.

20:44.990 --> 20:50.830
Yes they are...And maybe not,
depending on your point of view.

20:50.830 --> 20:54.000
Ahem. Excuse me...

20:54.000 --> 20:57.500
Everybody has a life, a daily life.

20:57.500 --> 21:00.340
There's no exception; they do.

21:00.340 --> 21:02.510
Conflict with their agent?

21:02.510 --> 21:05.380
It's none of our business!

21:08.350 --> 21:13.010
Of course, Eddy. These guys
are the next big thing in Japan.

21:14.520 --> 21:19.530
If we like them at the rehearsal,
yeah, we could play with them.

21:19.530 --> 21:23.760
Belle Ame...It means
"beautiful spirit" in French.

21:25.200 --> 21:27.390
Bugger off. Hit the road.

21:29.100 --> 21:31.370
-Jim, give me that!
-After all, Eddy is just a guy.

21:31.370 --> 21:32.640
-Hey! They're waiting for us.
-After all, Eddy is just a guy.

21:32.640 --> 21:35.710
-Why are you saying this now? Shit!
-But, that makes Dying Breed appealing.

21:35.710 --> 21:40.810
-What shall we do? That's irresponsible.
Hey Jim! What are you filming!?
-On top of that, Matt is wild.

21:42.220 --> 21:46.720
Like a river flowing,
inspiration always flows from my mind.

21:46.720 --> 21:50.890
-Hey! Dancing, dancing...Party man...
-Oh! He's a funny guy.

21:50.890 --> 21:55.830
-Happy birthday to you...
-Happy birthday to you...
-Happy birthday to you...

21:59.070 --> 22:03.570
Sometimes, there comes a special day,
while they're on tour.

22:03.570 --> 22:05.540
It's a beautiful scene.

22:06.570 --> 22:10.740
Tokyo...a city of noise
and chaos. Techno-city.

22:10.740 --> 22:11.580
Come on!

22:11.580 --> 22:14.250
They had a live here, as well.

22:14.250 --> 22:16.410
In the evening, with the shining moon...

22:18.090 --> 22:21.540
They met a boy. It was
a very special event.

22:38.370 --> 22:40.530
I felt like something great...

22:41.540 --> 22:42.940
...was about to happen.

22:50.580 --> 22:52.680
Another minute

22:52.680 --> 22:55.380
Feelin' so fine

22:57.690 --> 22:59.920
You turn the freeze

22:59.920 --> 23:02.650
into warm light

23:04.760 --> 23:08.230
Had a premonition

23:08.230 --> 23:10.900
I've been waitin' ever since

23:10.900 --> 23:14.400
My world comin' down

23:14.400 --> 23:17.200
It's got me spinnin' 'round

23:18.980 --> 23:25.150
If you really wanna fly

23:25.150 --> 23:27.910
you gotta let go

23:40.160 --> 23:42.500
Simply the most

23:42.500 --> 23:44.530
big sensation

23:44.530 --> 23:47.340
(once you're here you won't go back)

23:47.340 --> 23:49.610
She's really pretty

23:49.610 --> 23:51.610
One-eyed vision

23:51.610 --> 23:54.440
(lose the fear it don't come back)

23:54.440 --> 23:57.950
Little sister showed me

23:57.950 --> 24:00.620
Really took me for a ride

24:00.620 --> 24:02.280
My world comin' down

24:02.280 --> 24:05.620
(once you're here you won't go back)

24:05.620 --> 24:09.650
(lose the fear it don't come back)

24:13.760 --> 24:16.330
That Sato lady was funny, wasn't she?

24:16.330 --> 24:20.200
"Live 20
'Grateful Sound'”

24:16.330 --> 24:20.200
Next episode: Grateful Sound!
Will Beck be able to perform?
